A||||11||brian43||v8 Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||brian43||05-26-2001||04:49 PM||||On <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>  it says in the faq <BR>Q. Do I need to cut or stretch the frame? <P>A. No, our kit is designed for a "no frame cutting" installation. The V-8 Chevy engine will fit in any stock Fiero engine compartment. <P>Well here is mine<BR>Q. I want to build a kit car that you have to stretch the frame 11" can I still use his v8 kit?<P>A.?<BR>I emailed him, but I would kinda like to know right now. Any one done a strech to their fiero and used this v8 kit? Thanks,<BR>brian<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||BV MotorSports||05-26-2001||05:05 PM||||For an 11inch stretch you must be working on a Lambo kit???<P>Yeah you could use archies kit cause the engine doesnt move in the chassis since the cradle is moved back (and the engine is mounted to this). Im not gonna say anything bad about archies or anyone elses v8 kit but you would be much happier with the fit and finish of a 3.8sc. The money you save on NOT buying the v8 kit would pay to buy the supercharged 3.8 and most of the few things needed for the swap. <BR>I have built v8 fieros and I am telling you now....they really arent ummmmm ..... all that wonderfull. Braging rights aside.<P>If you want a v8, hey go for it...but be prepared for compromises.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||05-26-2001||05:33 PM||||If your going to do an 11" stretch, forget the Archie kit and put the V8 in longitudinally with a Porsche transaxle. Then you can abuse it all you want and not worry about the transmission breaking; you'll also have more room for headers, exhaust, and maintenance. You could also go with a big block if you go longitudinal.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero4never||05-26-2001||06:49 PM|||| Big Block in a fiero? Sounds like you have a death wish <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P> I'm prety sure the weight of a 454 would make turning at high speeds deadly.<P> Would be fun though.||||reg||1
