Z||000010||MoneypitGT||05-27-2001||06:45 PM||||You could also use a big block setup out of an olds tornado or caddy eldo. Those engine/tranny combos are cheap and then you can beat the hell out of the car with basically no worry. My 2 cents<BR>   Chris<P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||1
Z||000011||Dave Gunsul||05-27-2001||11:40 PM||||Will, I don't understand why you think that your porch   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> tranny and long mounted engine<BR>is better than Archies set up.<BR>There are at least two 450+ HP V8's in our club with Archies kit that haven't broken anything and are equipped with headers and<BR>stock 5-speeds.<BR>As for how much abuse they will take; have you ever taken a ride with Archie?? I think<BR>that he has proven that his set-up will take<BR>a lot of abuse.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I almost forgot about the maintenance aspect.<BR>Archies V8 set-up (even with headers) is easyer to work on than a stock V6.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 05-27-2001).]||||reg||1
